Description: Add AM_GNU_GETTEXT_REQUIRE_VERSION to fix autopoint FTBFS
 configure.in calls AM_GNU_GETTEXT (turned into AM_GNU_GETTEXT([external]) by
 gettext_external.diff) but never declares a gettext infrastructure version.
 Modern autopoint (gettext >= 0.18; sid currently ships 0.26) then falls back
 to the pre-versioning 0.10.x scheme, requests the long-removed
 gettext-0.10.32 layout and aborts autoreconf with "requires the
 infrastructure from gettext-0.10.32 but this version is older". Declaring a
 modern minimum via AM_GNU_GETTEXT_REQUIRE_VERSION([0.19.8]) gives autopoint a
 valid version to work from; the newer gettext installed on the build host is
 used at build time.
Author: Martin A. Godisch <godisch@debian.org>
Last-Update: 2026-06-04
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- lrzsz-0.12.21rc.orig/configure.in
+++ lrzsz-0.12.21rc/configure.in
@@ -268,6 +268,15 @@
 AC_SUBST(LDFLAGS)
 AC_SUBST(LIBS)
 
+dnl Declare the minimum GNU gettext infrastructure version that autopoint
+dnl must provide. This line is required by modern autopoint (gettext >= 0.18):
+dnl when it is missing, autopoint falls back to the pre-versioning 0.10.x
+dnl scheme, decides that the (no longer shipped) gettext-0.10.32 layout is
+dnl needed, and aborts autoreconf. 0.19.8 is the first release providing the
+dnl AM_GNU_GETTEXT_REQUIRE_VERSION macro itself, so it is a safe minimum; the
+dnl newer gettext actually installed on the build host is used at build time.
+AM_GNU_GETTEXT_REQUIRE_VERSION([0.19.8])
+
 AM_GNU_GETTEXT([external])
 
 AC_DEFINE_UNQUOTED(LOCALEDIR,"$prefix/$DATADIRNAME")
